WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.127
A strong reshape project includes validation.

00:00:03.127 --> 00:00:05.457
State the grain at every stage.

00:00:05.457 --> 00:00:09.432
Compare additive totals. Document the NULL policy.

00:00:09.432 --> 00:00:12.777
Confirm that expected categories and months are present.

00:00:12.777 --> 00:00:18.862
These checks make the transformation reproducible and reduce the chance of silent data loss.

00:00:18.862 --> 00:00:24.307
Connect this idea to a survey project reshaping question responses for analysis.

00:00:24.307 --> 00:00:29.767
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:37.097
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:37.097 --> 00:00:42.822
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:42.822 --> 00:00:48.800
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
